Znao si!

1213
01:45:03.220 --> 01:45:04.560
A nisi nam rekao!

1214
01:45:04.900 --> 01:45:07.500
Da sam ti rekao. ne bi izabrao ovaj put.

1215
01:45:07.700 --> 01:45:10.120
I ti ljudi bi još bili živi!

1216
01:45:10.360 --> 01:45:11.640
Ne! Svi bismo bili mrtvi.

1217
01:45:12.200 --> 01:45:13.240
Nisi imao pravo!

1218
01:45:13.440 --> 01:45:14.520
Imao sam svako pravo.

1219
01:45:14.980 --> 01:45:16.420
I svaka odgovornost.

1220
01:45:16.940 --> 01:45:18.980
Whirlpool bi uništio brod

1221
01:45:18.980 --> 01:45:19.800
i svi mi!

1222
01:45:20.060 --> 01:45:21.100
Ovako živimo!

1223
01:45:21.280 --> 01:45:22.380
Neki od nas žive!

1224
01:45:22.580 --> 01:45:23.040
Da!

1225
01:45:26.800 --> 01:45:28.680
Što vam je još Tirezije rekao?

1226
01:45:40.300 --> 01:45:41.620
Ja ću staviti tamo.

1227
01:45:44.180 --> 01:45:45.880
Ne možemo tamo sletjeti.

1228
01:45:46.060 --> 01:45:47.500
To je otok boga sunca.

1229
01:45:47.840 --> 01:45:48.720
Trebamo popravke!

1230
01:45:50.340 --> 01:45:51.880
Ovi ljudi su iscrpljeni!

1231
01:45:52.160 --> 01:45:53.600
Izgubio sam šest brodskih drugova!

1232
01:45:54.140 --> 01:45:54.940
Ti ćeš staviti.

1233
01:45:55.080 --> 01:45:56.820
Odmorit ću se na suhom.

1234
01:45:56.820 --> 01:45:58.220
Svi ćete umrijeti!

1235
01:46:00.980 --> 01:46:03.360
Pitali ste me što mi je Tirezije rekao.

1236
01:46:03.980 --> 01:46:05.720
Rekao je da ćete svi umrijeti.

1237
01:46:06.240 --> 01:46:09.920
Ako zakolješ stoku boga sunca.

1238
01:46:10.080 --> 01:46:11.640
koji pasu na tom otoku.

1239
01:46:11.880 --> 01:46:12.660
svi ćete umrijeti.

1240
01:46:16.930 --> 01:46:17.870
To je u redu.

1241
01:46:18.810 --> 01:46:19.870
Ubacit ćemo.

1242
01:46:20.650 --> 01:46:22.270
Sami ćemo skuhati namirnice.

1243
01:46:22.590 --> 01:46:23.390
Brat ćemo voće.

1244
01:46:23.530 --> 01:46:24.150
Donijet ćemo vodu.

1245
01:46:24.150 --> 01:46:24.810
Ubacit ćemo.

1246
01:46:24.810 --> 01:46:25.210
Ništa više.

1247
01:46:26.710 --> 01:46:27.690
Zakuni se na to.

1248
01:46:28.410 --> 01:46:29.290
Svi vi.

1249
01:46:43.510 --> 01:46:44.050
Vidjeti?

1250
01:46:45.330 --> 01:46:46.910
Vjetar nas je odmah odnio.

1251
01:46:47.990 --> 01:46:49.090
Odmorit ćemo se.

1252
01:46:49.750 --> 01:46:50.870
obaviti popravke.

1253
01:46:51.250 --> 01:46:52.950
i krenuti čim se vjetar promijeni.

1254
01:46:54.110 --> 01:46:55.030
Zgrabi to svjetlo.

1255
01:47:06.180 --> 01:47:07.980
Je li ekipa održala obećanje?

1256
01:47:09.260 --> 01:47:09.820
Da.

1257
01:47:10.920 --> 01:47:12.180
Dugo vremena.

1258
01:47:13.900 --> 01:47:15.620
Ali vjetar se nije mijenjao.

1259
01:47:15.900 --> 01:47:17.620
Postojani kopneni povjetarac

1260
01:47:17.620 --> 01:47:19.540
što nam je olakšalo slijetanje

1261
01:47:22.060 --> 01:47:23.860
onemogućio odlazak.

1262
01:47:27.990 --> 01:47:29.670
I ponestalo nam je namirnica.

1263
01:47:32.870 --> 01:47:33.390
Ići!

1264
01:48:36.420 --> 01:48:38.180
Jesi li mislio da jedeš tiho.

1265
01:48:38.360 --> 01:48:39.500
bog sunca ne bi primijetio?

1266
01:48:39.940 --> 01:48:41.440
Mislili smo da nećete primijetiti.

1267
01:48:42.400 --> 01:48:43.540
Ja nisam problem.

1268
01:48:43.900 --> 01:48:45.080
Želio sam da živiš.

1269
01:48:51.200 --> 01:48:52.220
Tyresius ti je rekao.

1270
01:48:52.720 --> 01:48:53.540
Cersei ti je rekla.

1271
01:48:53.620 --> 01:48:54.480
Bogovi su ti rekli.

1272
01:48:55.380 --> 01:48:57.720
Vi bogovi ne govorite onako kako mi razumijemo.

1273
01:48:57.720 --> 01:48:59.440
Tko ne razumije bol?

1274
01:49:00.500 --> 01:49:01.260
Ili krv?

1275
01:49:01.380 --> 01:49:01.740
Ili smrt?

1276
01:49:02.740 --> 01:49:04.020
Kad gledaš kako tvoj čovjek umire.

1277
01:49:04.080 --> 01:49:04.660
vidiš li šansu.

1278
01:49:04.700 --> 01:49:05.620
ili vidiš posljedicu?

1279
01:49:06.520 --> 01:49:07.600
Vidim posljedicu.

1280
01:49:07.940 --> 01:49:08.840
Vidim svoj neuspjeh.

1281
01:49:09.540 --> 01:49:11.220
Što ako njihova smrt nije tvoj neuspjeh.

1282
01:49:11.340 --> 01:49:11.700
ali njihov?

1283
01:49:12.460 --> 01:49:13.240
Ja ih vodim.

1284
01:49:14.960 --> 01:49:16.040
Ja sam ih doveo ovamo.

1285
01:49:16.740 --> 01:49:17.600
A tko vas je vodio?

1286
01:49:19.140 --> 01:49:20.920
Zašto se stavljaš iznad bogova?

1287
01:49:21.000 --> 01:49:22.380
Zašto preuzimate odgovornost?

1288
01:49:23.640 --> 01:49:25.060
Zašto ne želiš ići kući?

1289
01:49:25.380 --> 01:49:26.560
Što očekujete?

1290
01:49:28.400 --> 01:49:29.900
Ponestalo im je hrane.

1291
01:49:31.040 --> 01:49:32.100
Imaj malo sažaljenja.

1292
01:49:32.280 --> 01:49:35.100
Moja šteta je ono što nas je dovelo na ovaj prokleti otok.

1293
01:49:35.280 --> 01:49:36.520
Rekao sam ti što će se dogoditi.

1294
01:49:36.780 --> 01:49:37.420
Da. jesi.

1295
01:49:38.200 --> 01:49:41.120
I odlučili smo da ćemo se radije utopiti nego gladovati.

1296
01:49:47.490 --> 01:49:48.970
Pa. sada je naša prilika.

1297
01:49:49.470 --> 01:49:50.510
Vjetar je prestao!

1298
01:49:50.810 --> 01:49:51.590
Vjetar je prestao!

1299
01:49:55.370 --> 01:49:57.210
Zatišje je bilo dovoljno dugo

1300
01:49:57.210 --> 01:49:59.150
da nas namami na Posejdonov ocean.

1301
01:50:00.430 --> 01:50:01.770
Pod Zeusovim nebom.

1302
01:51:53.400 --> 01:51:56.820
Zadnje čega se sjećam bila je Zeusova gruba ruka.

1303
01:52:41.770 --> 01:52:43.430
Ne znam što se dogodilo mojim ljudima.

1304
01:52:43.670 --> 01:52:44.410
Da. imaš.

1305
01:52:46.770 --> 01:52:48.330
Upravo ono što ste im rekli da će se dogoditi.

1306
01:52:48.330 --> 01:52:50.970
Na tvoju sam obalu isplivao sam.

1307
01:52:51.230 --> 01:52:53.070
Izbacilo te na moju obalu

1308
01:52:53.070 --> 01:52:54.690
s nekim svojim brodom

1309
01:52:54.690 --> 01:52:55.770
i nitko od vaše posade.

1310
01:52:57.890 --> 01:52:59.910
Napola mrtav. bez svijesti.

1311
01:53:22.650 --> 01:53:26.490
Danima sam te gledao izgubljenog

1312
01:53:27.170 --> 01:53:28.350
u tjedne.

1313
01:53:29.110 --> 01:53:31.730
Znao sam da će ti Lotus olakšati buđenje

1314
01:53:33.350 --> 01:53:36.150
tako da je tvoja bol bila više tijela nego uma.

1315
01:53:38.730 --> 01:53:39.850
I jest.

1316
01:53:42.410 --> 01:53:44.270
Toliko ti se svidjelo.

1317
01:53:45.390 --> 01:53:47.390
Tako si ga rado pojeo.

1318
01:53:51.150 --> 01:53:52.750
I kao što sam brinuo za tebe.

1319
01:53:53.310 --> 01:53:54.050
Hvala.

1320
01:53:54.770 --> 01:53:55.850
Zavolio sam te.

1321
01:54:01.440 --> 01:54:02.940
Koliko sam dugo ovdje?

1322
01:54:05.240 --> 01:54:08.080
Stalno sam si govorio da ti to prestanem davati.

1323
01:54:08.240 --> 01:54:09.960
Da si bio dovoljno jak da se sjetiš.

1324
01:54:09.960 --> 01:54:11.180
Koliko dugo. Calypso?

1325
01:54:11.280 --> 01:54:12.400
Bio si tako sretan.

1326
01:54:12.580 --> 01:54:13.320
Bio si sretan.

1327
01:54:13.440 --> 01:54:15.020
Bili smo tako sretni.

1328
01:54:15.220 --> 01:54:16.020
Godinama.

1329
01:54:16.540 --> 01:54:16.960
godine?

1330
01:54:23.970 --> 01:54:25.030
Sedam godina.

1331
01:54:25.910 --> 01:54:27.930
Nahranio si me lotosovim cvijetom

1332
01:54:27.930 --> 01:54:29.710
i držao me zarobljenim.

1333
01:54:30.010 --> 01:54:31.370
Spasio sam ti život.

1334
01:54:31.970 --> 01:54:33.610
Obnovio sam tvoje tijelo.

1335
01:54:33.750 --> 01:54:35.030
Jednostavno se nisam mogao sabrati

1336
01:54:35.030 --> 01:54:36.310
da obnovite svoj um.

1337
01:54:37.570 --> 01:54:39.030
Bio si sretan.

1338
01:54:39.810 --> 01:54:40.890
Vaše srce

1339
01:54:40.890 --> 01:54:43.090
uvijek je bio negdje drugdje.

1340
01:54:44.310 --> 01:54:45.410
I tvoj um

1341
01:54:45.410 --> 01:54:46.890
morao slijediti

1342
01:54:46.890 --> 01:54:47.470
eventualno.

1343
01:54:48.790 --> 01:54:49.790
Kako si mogao?

1344
01:54:50.250 --> 01:54:51.610
Lotosovi oblaci

1345
01:54:51.610 --> 01:54:52.310
uma

1346
01:54:52.310 --> 01:54:53.670
i soči bunar

1347
01:54:53.670 --> 01:54:54.690
ali se ne mijenja

1348
01:54:54.690 --> 01:54:55.570
tko si ti.

1349
01:54:56.090 --> 01:54:57.250
Nisi bio spreman

1350
01:54:57.250 --> 01:54:58.030
otići kući

1351
01:54:58.030 --> 01:54:59.070
iz bilo kojeg razloga.

1352
01:54:59.490 --> 01:55:00.550
I am now.

1353
01:55:02.030 --> 01:55:03.290
As I always knew

1354
01:55:03.290 --> 01:55:03.890
you would be.

1355
01:55:04.870 --> 01:55:05.310
How?

1356
01:55:05.750 --> 01:55:07.270
You were clutching something

1357
01:55:07.270 --> 01:55:08.370
when I found you.

1358
01:55:08.830 --> 01:55:09.810
Your hand wouldn't open

1359
01:55:09.810 --> 01:55:10.370
for weeks.

1360
01:55:11.130 --> 01:55:12.410
You'd call out.

1361
01:55:13.150 --> 01:55:14.450
Mostly to Athena

1362
01:55:14.450 --> 01:55:16.030
but sometimes

1363
01:55:16.030 --> 01:55:16.750
you would say

1364
01:55:16.750 --> 01:55:17.450
another name.

1365
01:55:36.730 --> 01:55:38.230
Help me go home.

1366
01:55:38.830 --> 01:55:39.930
I am.

1367
01:55:41.170 --> 01:55:42.150
You're a man

1368
01:55:42.150 --> 01:55:43.030
who needs to control

1369
01:55:43.030 --> 01:55:43.630
his fate

1370
01:55:45.010 --> 01:55:46.410
but you cannot control

1371
01:55:46.410 --> 01:55:46.830
this.

1372
01:55:50.050 --> 01:55:51.370
You must give yourself

1373
01:55:51.370 --> 01:55:52.150
to the storm

1374
01:55:52.150 --> 01:55:53.750
give yourself

1375
01:55:53.750 --> 01:55:54.650
to Poseidon

1376
01:55:56.010 --> 01:55:57.450
and take your punishment.

1377
01:56:00.330 --> 01:56:01.510
Zeus won't let him

1378
01:56:01.510 --> 01:56:01.990
kill you.

1379
01:56:05.610 --> 01:56:06.930
Give up the fight

1380
01:56:06.930 --> 01:56:08.050
give up control

1381
01:56:08.050 --> 01:56:08.870
and live

1382
01:56:11.790 --> 01:56:12.670
and to leave

1383
01:56:12.670 --> 01:56:13.190
a fate

1384
01:56:13.190 --> 01:56:14.690
you've never yet

1385
01:56:14.690 --> 01:56:15.870
made Odysseus.

1386
01:57:08.150 --> 01:57:08.730
Odysseus.

1387
01:57:16.960 --> 01:57:17.980
Where am I?

1388
01:57:20.120 --> 01:57:21.220
Don't you recognize

1389
01:57:21.220 --> 01:57:21.920
your own home?

1390
01:58:01.220 --> 01:58:02.540
Zeus welcomes you

1391
01:58:02.540 --> 01:58:02.940
strangers.

1392
01:58:04.120 --> 01:58:05.280
How many are you?

1393
01:58:06.040 --> 01:58:06.840
Half a dozen.

1394
01:58:07.760 --> 01:58:08.500
Need of a meal?

1395
01:58:08.980 --> 01:58:09.900
And supplies

1396
01:58:09.900 --> 01:58:11.480
for the road.

1397
01:58:12.080 --> 01:58:13.040
Where are you headed?

1398
01:58:13.380 --> 01:58:14.440
We need pigs.

1399
01:58:14.840 --> 01:58:15.840
We're going all the way

1400
01:58:15.840 --> 01:58:16.500
to Pylos.

1401
01:58:16.900 --> 01:58:17.980
Are you pilgrims?

1402
01:58:18.940 --> 01:58:20.600
Do we look like pilgrims?

1403
01:58:20.600 --> 01:58:21.960
I don't see well.

1404
01:58:23.200 --> 01:58:24.120
Zeus demands

1405
01:58:24.120 --> 01:58:25.080
I offer you a meal

1406
01:58:25.080 --> 01:58:25.860
but these pigs

1407
01:58:25.860 --> 01:58:26.940
aren't mine to sell.

1408
01:58:27.220 --> 01:58:27.940
Oh don't worry.

1409
01:58:28.720 --> 01:58:29.640
We're not paying.

1410
01:58:33.260 --> 01:58:34.460
Give my greetings

1411
01:58:34.460 --> 01:58:35.240
to your mother.

1412
01:58:38.540 --> 01:58:39.780
Tell her I'm sorry.

1413
01:58:40.160 --> 01:58:41.460
I'm sorry for Troy.

1414
01:58:50.460 --> 01:58:51.440
I'm sorry I had

1415
01:58:51.440 --> 01:58:52.560
no news from your father.

1416
01:58:53.000 --> 01:58:54.000
No. you had news.

1417
01:58:54.440 --> 01:58:55.600
Not where he is

1418
01:58:55.600 --> 01:58:56.320
but who he is.

1419
01:58:57.820 --> 01:58:58.980
And now more than ever

1420
01:58:58.980 --> 01:58:59.660
I hope to one day

1421
01:58:59.660 --> 01:59:00.080
meet him.

1422
01:59:05.130 --> 01:59:06.130
Where are you

1423
01:59:06.130 --> 01:59:07.350
watchdogs old man?

1424
01:59:11.800 --> 01:59:13.580
I'm burning their bodies.

1425
01:59:18.170 --> 01:59:19.650
Can Zeus sacrifice you

1426
01:59:19.650 --> 01:59:20.870
food and drake stranger?

1427
01:59:21.810 --> 01:59:22.870
Were you attacked?

1428
01:59:23.630 --> 01:59:24.710
The dog saved

1429
01:59:24.710 --> 01:59:25.430
your farm heads.

1430
01:59:25.950 --> 01:59:26.830
Oh. it burned.

1431
01:59:26.830 --> 01:59:27.810
his brothers first.

1432
01:59:30.690 --> 01:59:32.270
What happened to Ithaca?

1433
01:59:33.190 --> 01:59:33.890
Darkness.

1434
01:59:34.350 --> 01:59:35.350
the law of Zeus

1435
01:59:35.350 --> 01:59:36.670
completely smashed to pieces.

1436
01:59:36.670 --> 01:59:38.430
a kingdom

1437
01:59:38.430 --> 01:59:39.350
without a king

1438
01:59:39.350 --> 01:59:40.390
since my master

1439
01:59:40.390 --> 01:59:40.870
deceased.

1440
01:59:41.130 --> 01:59:41.950
Your master?

1441
01:59:43.290 --> 01:59:44.090
Odysseus.

1442
01:59:44.790 --> 01:59:46.470
Hero of the Trojan War.

1443
01:59:48.550 --> 01:59:50.370
But Odysseus is still alive.

1444
01:59:50.670 --> 01:59:53.690
Not anymore!

1445
01:59:53.950 --> 01:59:54.430
Not anymore!

1446
01:59:54.430 --> 01:59:55.910
Not anymore!

1447
01:59:56.290 --> 01:59:56.610
Not anymore!

1448
01:59:56.610 --> 01:59:57.530
Not anymore!

1449
01:59:57.850 --> 01:59:58.170
Not anymore!

1450
01:59:59.350 --> 01:59:59.910
Telemachus.

1451
02:00:00.450 --> 02:00:01.010
Telemachus.

1452
02:00:02.410 --> 02:00:02.970
Telemachus.

1453
02:00:03.150 --> 02:00:03.930
He is in danger.

1454
02:00:04.310 --> 02:00:05.430
He is in danger.

1455
02:00:05.430 --> 02:00:06.450
And I can't help him.

1456
02:00:06.870 --> 02:00:07.830
There must be more.

1457
02:00:07.830 --> 02:00:08.330
in this

1458
02:00:08.330 --> 02:00:08.930
because it would

1459
02:00:08.930 --> 02:00:10.350
help the son of Odysseus.

1460
02:00:10.550 --> 02:00:11.170
The palace is

1461
02:00:11.170 --> 02:00:12.510
controlled by potential partners.

1462
02:00:13.150 --> 02:00:14.630
No one is loyal anymore

1463
02:00:14.630 --> 02:00:15.670
to Odysseus.

1464
02:00:16.810 --> 02:00:18.010
And what about the queen?

1465
02:00:19.010 --> 02:00:26.790
Beautiful. wise Penelope. held hostage by the worst of men. will soon be forced to marry.

1466
02:00:26.790 --> 02:00:28.990
What could she do without even her son?

1467
02:00:29.430 --> 02:00:30.270
Here. drink.

1468
02:00:35.260 --> 02:00:37.060
What is the danger for Telemachus?

1469
02:00:37.800 --> 02:00:39.980
He is on his way back from Sparta.

1470
02:00:41.060 --> 02:00:45.860
The suitors sent bandits to Pylos to ambush him in the temple.

1471
02:00:46.680 --> 02:00:48.080
Give me something to eat for the road.

1472
02:00:49.600 --> 02:00:51.540
You will never catch up with the bandits.

1473
02:00:52.000 --> 02:00:55.140
If I can reach Pylos before Telemachus arrives. I can warn him.

1474
02:00:55.780 --> 02:00:56.960
Why are you helping?

1475
02:00:57.820 --> 02:00:59.700
If I tell you. don't get angry.

1476
02:01:00.260 --> 02:01:02.300
I served with Odysseus in Troy.

1477
02:01:02.540 --> 02:01:03.060
Real?

1478
02:01:04.480 --> 02:01:06.180
He was a strict teacher.

1479
02:01:06.380 --> 02:01:07.320
Oh. but rightly so.

1480
02:01:08.920 --> 02:01:10.880
Honest and worth following.

1481
02:01:12.240 --> 02:01:13.240
You loved him.

1482
02:01:14.180 --> 02:01:15.280
Like a son.

1483
02:01:16.760 --> 02:01:18.580
Well. he's not dead.

1484
02:01:19.120 --> 02:01:20.800
Is he coming home?

1485
02:01:21.880 --> 02:01:22.460
Soon.

1486
02:01:23.260 --> 02:01:24.580
Take revenge.

1487
02:01:26.940 --> 02:01:28.280
Take everything with you.

1488
02:01:37.660 --> 02:01:38.600
I'll talk.

1489
02:01:38.840 --> 02:01:40.700
We don't want people to know where you are.

1490
02:01:40.920 --> 02:01:42.540
Maybe we shouldn't have brought a guard.

1491
02:01:43.000 --> 02:01:45.240
We'll be glad we did it if we run into problems along the way.

1492
02:02:05.460 --> 02:02:06.400
Find that beggar.

1493
02:02:22.540 --> 02:02:23.980
Your men should wait out here.

1494
02:02:24.220 --> 02:02:25.080
Also the weapons.

1495
02:02:42.590 --> 02:02:43.830
Zeus welcomes you strangers.

1496
02:02:44.450 --> 02:02:45.590
Have you made a long journey?

1497
02:02:46.070 --> 02:02:47.150
Not that far.

1498
02:02:48.470 --> 02:02:50.350
You are here to rest tonight.

1499
02:02:52.430 --> 02:02:54.550
We are here to make a sacrifice to Athena.

1500
02:02:56.710 --> 02:02:59.750
And any hospitality you can offer will likely be considered.

1501
02:03:00.210 --> 02:03:00.790
Naturally.

1502
02:03:01.030 --> 02:03:02.530
Away with that beggar!

1503
02:03:02.610 --> 02:03:03.830
He has a message for me.

1504
02:03:04.830 --> 02:03:06.070
He may have sent you.

1505
02:03:07.370 --> 02:03:08.130
Yes. sir.

1506
02:03:14.170 --> 02:03:15.430
Well. what's the message?

1507
02:03:16.910 --> 02:03:17.890
It's private.

1508
02:03:17.890 --> 02:03:19.390
These men are handsome.

1509
02:03:21.110 --> 02:03:22.250
These men are handsome.

1510
02:03:39.790 --> 02:03:41.870
This is your time to leave. old man.

1511
02:03:42.770 --> 02:03:43.430
Go away. stranger.

1512
02:03:46.170 --> 02:03:48.430
I already saved an old man this week.

1513
02:03:48.850 --> 02:03:50.030
But he was blind.

1514
02:03:50.030 --> 02:03:52.110
I won't spare them.

1515
02:03:52.570 --> 02:03:54.710
I won't spare them.

1516
02:04:30.820 --> 02:04:32.180
Not bad for a beggar.

1517
02:04:32.940 --> 02:04:34.260
No one is born a beggar.

1518
02:04:34.980 --> 02:04:37.880
We'll take this priest's robe and put it over your armor.

1519
02:04:40.180 --> 02:04:41.360
Help me with his body.

1520
02:04:41.640 --> 02:04:42.460
We have to leave him behind.

1521
02:04:43.080 --> 02:04:43.480
No.

1522
02:04:43.760 --> 02:04:44.800
We have to sneak out.

1523
02:04:45.580 --> 02:04:47.040
That's not how you honor the dead.

1524
02:04:47.200 --> 02:04:48.440
This is how you stay alive.

1525
02:04:48.640 --> 02:04:49.520
He was my teacher.

1526
02:04:50.880 --> 02:04:52.440
He could have been Athena in disguise.

1527
02:04:52.440 --> 02:04:53.740
His name was Mentor.

1528
02:04:54.380 --> 02:04:57.280
And when you're safe. we'll travel to the unknown west.

1529
02:04:57.780 --> 02:04:58.980
And we will honor him.

1530
02:04:59.460 --> 02:05:01.020
These men were sent by the suitors.

1531
02:05:01.480 --> 02:05:03.640
There will be more that we need to get on the road.

1532
02:05:03.940 --> 02:05:04.540
At night?

1533
02:05:04.840 --> 02:05:06.000
Safer than staying here.

1534
02:05:06.700 --> 02:05:08.700
Mentor is located in the heart of the oldest temple of Athena.

1535
02:05:09.280 --> 02:05:11.480
For now. we honor him with a fire.

1536
02:05:50.350 --> 02:05:52.210
How does a beggar come into contact with Mentor?

1537
02:05:52.390 --> 02:05:53.290
I told you so.

1538
02:05:53.470 --> 02:05:54.850
I have not always been a beggar.

1539
02:05:55.350 --> 02:05:56.750
You have a wise look.

1540
02:05:57.850 --> 02:05:58.410
The eyes of Athena.

1541
02:05:58.850 --> 02:05:59.750
You are gods and men.

1542
02:05:59.990 --> 02:06:01.010
You will only be disappointed.

1543
02:06:01.750 --> 02:06:03.410
Well. then tell me who you are.

1544
02:06:05.070 --> 02:06:06.370
My name is Sinon.

1545
02:06:07.070 --> 02:06:09.950
I am an old soldier who fought under your father in Troy.

1546
02:06:11.350 --> 02:06:12.350
Did you know my father?

1547
02:06:12.830 --> 02:06:15.930
I've been taking orders from him for longer than I can remember.

1548
02:06:16.930 --> 02:06:18.010
Wait. is he still alive?

1549
02:06:19.250 --> 02:06:20.090
He's still alive.

1550
02:06:21.870 --> 02:06:23.050
Where is he then?

1551
02:06:23.570 --> 02:06:23.930
Where is he then?

1552
02:06:23.930 --> 02:06:24.650
He's nearby.

1553
02:06:25.510 --> 02:06:27.590
He sent me ahead to assess the situation.

1554
02:06:29.190 --> 02:06:30.930
Well. mother won't believe it.

1555
02:06:31.170 --> 02:06:32.290
No. you can't tell her.

1556
02:06:33.530 --> 02:06:34.330
What. nothing?

1557
02:06:35.770 --> 02:06:36.490
Tell her.

1558
02:06:37.970 --> 02:06:38.590
Tell her.

1559
02:06:38.650 --> 02:06:40.330
Tell her he decided it's time she remarried.

1560
02:06:42.150 --> 02:06:43.790
He doesn't need to test my mother.

1561
02:06:43.910 --> 02:06:44.650
How can he doubt her?

1562
02:06:44.950 --> 02:06:45.690
He doesn't.

1563
02:06:46.290 --> 02:06:48.630
But she has every reason to have forgotten him.

1564
02:06:50.390 --> 02:06:52.050
Are there any loyal servants?

1565
02:06:53.270 --> 02:06:53.830
Some?

1566
02:06:55.230 --> 02:06:56.970
Well. he just shows himself all.

1567
02:06:58.430 --> 02:07:00.630
We need to gather the suitors at the palace.

1568
02:07:01.570 --> 02:07:02.830
That's never a problem.

1569
02:07:03.730 --> 02:07:05.050
You have gifts for Menelaus?

1570
02:07:05.050 --> 02:07:06.510
Yeah. on my ship.

1571
02:07:07.390 --> 02:07:07.670
Good.

1572
02:07:08.570 --> 02:07:09.790
Come back as a prince.

1573
02:07:10.510 --> 02:07:11.170
Call a banquet.

1574
02:07:11.990 --> 02:07:12.850
I'll be there.

1575
02:07:13.970 --> 02:07:15.390
What will you do at the banquet?

1576
02:07:16.350 --> 02:07:16.830
Beg.

1577
02:07:17.630 --> 02:07:19.710
The clearest view of a man is from below.

1578
02:07:21.730 --> 02:07:23.130
How many suitors are there?

1579
02:07:24.170 --> 02:07:24.650
Dozens.

1580
02:07:25.490 --> 02:07:27.430
If all of his men are like you. then...

1581
02:07:27.430 --> 02:07:28.550
He doesn't have any men.

1582
02:07:29.510 --> 02:07:30.510
But it's just you?

1583
02:07:32.010 --> 02:07:32.750
And you.

1584
02:07:39.090 --> 02:07:40.290
Telemachus is back.

1585
02:07:40.490 --> 02:07:40.730
What?

1586
02:07:40.910 --> 02:07:41.870
Telemachus is back.

1587
02:07:42.470 --> 02:07:43.650
Who's saying this?

1588
02:07:44.050 --> 02:07:45.450
Everyone's thinking of...

1589
02:07:45.450 --> 02:07:46.570
Where's Telemachus?

1590
02:07:47.110 --> 02:07:48.010
My queen!

1591
02:07:48.570 --> 02:07:49.950
Surely your place is up there.

1592
02:07:57.930 --> 02:07:58.950
Is it true?

1593
02:08:02.030 --> 02:08:02.990
You're home?

1594
02:08:04.170 --> 02:08:04.910
I'm back.

1595
02:08:05.910 --> 02:08:07.250
I thought tonight we could celebrate.

1596
02:08:08.070 --> 02:08:11.210
If we have anything left to celebrate with.

1597
02:08:12.830 --> 02:08:13.530
Don't worry.

1598
02:08:14.250 --> 02:08:17.210
My brave suitors will shower us with gifts to honor your return.

1599
02:08:17.610 --> 02:08:19.070
So glad to see your safe return.

1600
02:08:30.050 --> 02:08:31.370
Glad to see you on your feet.

1601
02:08:31.990 --> 02:08:33.970
It's about time we took you back to the palace.

1602
02:08:37.700 --> 02:08:38.980
What did you hear about your father?

1603
02:08:41.360 --> 02:08:41.760
Nothing.

1604
02:08:43.220 --> 02:08:46.420
Stories from the war. but no one knew what happened to him after he left Troy.

1605
02:08:47.000 --> 02:08:48.000
I'm sorry mom.

1606
02:08:49.440 --> 02:08:52.600
Everyone in Sparta is talking about a coming catastrophe.

1607
02:08:53.640 --> 02:08:57.660
An age of darkness brought on by people from the sea violating Zeus' law.

1608
02:08:57.900 --> 02:08:58.980
Then stories are true.

1609
02:08:59.280 --> 02:09:00.920
Our civilization is collapsing.

1610
02:09:01.620 --> 02:09:04.280
Menelaus is concerned that we can't raise an army with an empty throne.

1611
02:09:04.740 --> 02:09:06.080
So we came up with a plan.

1612
02:09:07.780 --> 02:09:08.500
What plan?

1613
02:09:10.940 --> 02:09:12.740
The one way to get the suitors to leave.

1614
02:09:15.300 --> 02:09:16.620
It's time for you to choose.

1615
02:09:20.660 --> 02:09:21.860
You want me to remarry?

1616
02:09:22.400 --> 02:09:25.200
If you remarry. the other suitors will leave.

1617
02:09:25.360 --> 02:09:27.060
And then I'm only dealing with one of them.

1618
02:09:27.380 --> 02:09:28.440
I'm almost of age.

1619
02:09:28.540 --> 02:09:31.380
I'll tell the elders that I learned of Odysseus' death in Sparta.

1620
02:09:32.640 --> 02:09:35.440
Menelaus will back me up and they'll let me assume the throne.

1621
02:09:35.440 --> 02:09:39.020
So you deny your father and I leave my home and go live with one of these snakes.

1622
02:09:39.220 --> 02:09:39.700
That's your plan.

1623
02:09:40.240 --> 02:09:41.240
Would you have a better one?

1624
02:09:44.300 --> 02:09:47.360
Lock the door. set afire. and burn the bastards.

1625
02:09:48.800 --> 02:09:52.280
Do you think if I remarry. life goes back to the way it was?

1626
02:09:53.380 --> 02:09:54.580
That world is gone.

1627
02:09:55.320 --> 02:09:58.280
And in this one. they're not giving up power to you.

1628
02:09:59.040 --> 02:09:59.840
Or Odysseus.

1629
02:09:59.840 --> 02:10:01.860
If he returned. he'd have to kill them.

1630
02:10:02.280 --> 02:10:03.200
Like you will.

1631
02:10:04.100 --> 02:10:07.340
If I kill them. their families will demand revenge.

1632
02:10:07.500 --> 02:10:08.400
I'd be exiled.

1633
02:10:09.380 --> 02:10:11.500
And without me. the throne will be lost.

1634
02:10:11.540 --> 02:10:13.040
Because only a man can sit on it.

1635
02:10:15.120 --> 02:10:16.020
Empty throne?

1636
02:10:17.700 --> 02:10:20.520
I've been sitting on that empty throne for 20 years!

1637
02:10:21.320 --> 02:10:24.220
My knowledge. my years of experience.

1638
02:10:24.420 --> 02:10:26.560
that's all nothing compared with the bristles on your chin!

1639
02:10:29.840 --> 02:10:30.700
Do you want peace?

1640
02:10:31.700 --> 02:10:32.960
Or do you want revenge?

1641
02:10:33.080 --> 02:10:34.020
I want Odysseus!

1642
02:10:37.340 --> 02:10:38.040
Sing!

1643
02:10:38.780 --> 02:10:40.320
Muse of a face!

1644
02:10:43.600 --> 02:10:44.720
A face!

1645
02:10:49.530 --> 02:10:50.160
A fleet!

1646
02:10:54.500 --> 02:10:55.760
A war!

1647
02:11:00.320 --> 02:11:01.160
At Troy!

1648
02:11:05.280 --> 02:11:07.280
Sing news of a man!

1649
02:11:11.160 --> 02:11:12.320
A man!

1650
02:11:16.900 --> 02:11:17.700
Let's go!

1651
02:11:21.780 --> 02:11:22.660
A British!

1652
02:11:27.080 --> 02:11:28.140
Ymaes. go ahead.

1653
02:11:35.360 --> 02:11:35.960
jacket.

1654
02:11:58.840 --> 02:12:00.780
You should bury him up on the cliffs.

1655
